cartridge "FIREFLIES/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' FIREFLIES - an original game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
'
' Dusk in a meadow. You carry a lantern; a swarm of fireflies follows its
' light. Lead them into the glass jar before dawn.
'
' Controls (either controller, joystick + side buttons; no keypad):
'   JOYSTICK   walk (8 directions); bushes, stumps, the pond, frogs and
'              jars are in the way
'   BUTTON     hold: the lantern shines bright - a wider light, a stronger
'              pull, a tighter swarm, bats flee it. It burns oil (bar at
'              the bottom right); empty, it must refill to a third first.
' Goal: fill the jar - deliver at least the fireflies shown by the dots at
' the bottom left before dawn (the moon bar at the top right).
' Score: a firefly in the jar is 10 x chain (chain: jars less than 1 s apart,
' up to x5); a firefly freed from a web 5; the whole swarm saved +200.
' Fireflies outside the light drift and stray (drawn dim); a wider light
' gathers them. Hazards: frogs puff their throat, then snap at fireflies
' near the pond; webs trap fireflies (walk into the web to free them before
' the spider comes, 5 s); gusts (night 3+, the HUD arrow blinks first)
' scatter the swarm; bats (night 4+) eat fireflies but flee a bright light.
' A night that ends short of the jar's dots costs a lantern (3, +1 every
' 4th night, max 5); the night is played again.
'
' Screen: Graphics II as a bitmap: rows 2-21 have one pattern per cell
' (name = cell), so each firefly is a glyph XORed into the background
' patterns by inline Z80 (FfGlyph: read-modify-write of VRAM; erase = the
' same XOR), in a 4x4 window kept inside its own cell: lit = a round 4x4 glow
' pulsing (0.94 Hz) with its 2x2 core, caught 2x2, stray 2x1, dim 1x1.
' No sprites for the swarm: no flicker.
' HUD rows 1 and 22 use 60 tiles kept in names 0-63 (third 0) and
' 192-255 (third 2). Sprites: the player (body + lantern), the frog's
' tongue, the bat: 4 in all, never more than 4 on a line.
' Flocking (FfFlies: a quarter of the swarm a frame, 4-frame steps; unlit
' ones every 8th frame, 8-frame steps): positions 8.8, velocities
' in 1/32 px a frame; a lit firefly steers to its own slot on a ring around
' the lantern (RingN/RingB tables, the ring turns slowly), unlit ones drift
' home with jitter; one neighbour a frame (separation; cohesion when both
' are unlit), flee from threat points (bat, tongue tip), wind; distance =
' max + min / 2; no multiply anywhere in the frame.

